<title>FRANCE: EU adds 79,000 T to German barley export quota.</title>
<headline>EU adds 79,000 T to German barley export quota.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday increased by 79,000 tonnes the quota of German intervention barley available for export, France's grain office ONIC said.</p>
<p>The EU's grain committee also allocated 48,000 tonnes of barley to Denmark, 42,000 tonnes to Finland, and 13,000 to Sweden for export to non-EU countries, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
